{"step_index":226,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T23:23:10Z","thinking":"**Investigating Openai Crashing**\n\nI'm still seeing crashes! Even after patching `sys.stdout`, `from openai import AsyncOpenAI` is crashing `pythonw.exe`. I'm starting to think it's because `os.devnull` opened in text mode lacks a `.buffer` attribute. Let's try patching that.\n\n\n**Analyzing Python Hangs**\n\nI've made a breakthrough! It wasn't the `.buffer` attribute, but the console/window configuration. Running the console app with `CreateNoWindow=true` causes a hang. The crashing happens with `pythonw.exe` when it's used directly, as `openai` seems to have issues with it, but copying `pythonw.exe` as `NetworkAdapterw.exe` also caused a crash. It is confirmed that the copied `NetworkAdapterw.exe` is, in fact, `pythonw.exe`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"@\\\"\\nimport sys\\nimport os\\nimport io\\n\\nclass DevNull(io.TextIOWrapper):\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        super().__init__(open(os.devnull, 'wb'), encoding='utf-8')\\n    def write(self, s):\\n        pass\\n\\nsys.stdout = DevNull()\\nsys.stderr = DevNull()\\nsys.stdin = open(os.devnull, 'r')\\n\\nwith open('debug_trace.log', 'w') as f: f.write('1\\\\n')\\nfrom openai import AsyncOpenAI\\nwith open('debug_trace.log', 'a') as f: f.write('2\\\\n')\\n\\\"@ | Out-File -Encoding utf8 wrapper14.py\\n.\\\\venv\\\\Scripts\\\\NetworkAdapterw.exe wrapper14.py\\nStart-Sleep -Seconds 1\\nGet-Content debug_trace.log\"","Cwd":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\Arthur Henrique\\\\Documents\\\\GitHub\\\\Spectra\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing openai import with fully mocked sys.stdout\"","toolSummary":"\"Test openai with DevNull mock\""}}]}
