{"step_index":230,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T23:23:34Z","thinking":"**Analyzing the Output**\n\nOkay, so I just ran the script, expecting \"Hello\" to be printed, but nothing showed up. My initial thought was PowerShell handle issues, but that's not it. I'm focusing on the `Out-File -Encoding utf8` and `.\\venv\\Scripts` commands and their impact. I'm trying to figure out why the output isn't going where I expect.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Robustly fix sys.stdout and sys.stderr in main.py to handle invalid handles when running in no-console mode with python.exe.\"","EndLine":"18","Instruction":"\"Replace the sys.stdout/stderr patching with a robust one that catches OSErrors on write.\"","ReplacementContent":"\"import os\\nimport sys\\n\\ntry:\\n    import shutil\\n    import time\\n    from pathlib import Path\\n\\n# Robustly fix invalid handles when running without a console\\nfor attr in ('stdout', 'stderr'):\\n    stream = getattr(sys, attr)\\n    is_valid = False\\n    if stream is not None:\\n        try:\\n            stream.write('')\\n            stream.flush()\\n            is_valid = True\\n            if hasattr(stream, 'reconfigure'):\\n                stream.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8')\\n        except OSError:\\n            pass\\n    if not is_valid:\\n        setattr(sys, attr, open(os.devnull, 'w'))\\n\\nif sys.stdin is None:\\n    sys.stdin = open(os.devnull, 'r')\"","StartLine":"1","TargetContent":"\"import os\\nimport sys\\n\\ntry:\\n    import shutil\\n    import time\\n    from pathlib import Path\\n\\n# Force UTF-8 for standard output/error, and fix NoneType crash in pythonw.exe\\nif sys.stdout is None:\\n    sys.stdout = open(os.devnull, 'w')\\nelif hasattr(sys.stdout, 'reconfigure'):\\n    try:\\n        sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8')\\n    except Exception:\\n        pass\\n\\nif sys.stderr is None: